  "notes": [
    "Compatible subset; the original STLport release is not uniquely identified.",
    "Vendored excerpts preserve node/member declarations, swap and six Rb_global algorithm bodies.",
    "Configuration macros are expanded for the supported namespace/calling convention; unrelated declarations are omitted.",
    "Explicit-instantiation translation units are project integration files, not recovered original file boundaries.",
    "The first 86 container fragments use only builtin, STLport and pointer types; game pointees are forward declarations.",
    "Native new keeps bad_alloc::what as a declaration, without its unused inline body/string; no retained instantiation calls it. This is an integration boundary, not recovered original header text.",
    "All container-generated allocated output is text, checked completely. No unused generated data is dropped.",
    "The selected profile disables exceptions, iostreams, wide-character facilities and threading; it uses new/delete allocation and the _STL namespace. Other profiles remain unverified.",
    "A further 44 container fragments use scoped game storage declarations and two recovered comparator behaviors; see docs/GameContainers.md for exact evidence, unknowns and restrictions. The separate PathFindingNetwork copy constructor is reconstructed game code."
  ],
